            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary thrombosis as the manifestation of the antiphospholipid syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>327-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present 3 cases of antiphospholipid syndrome with thrombosis in the coronary circulation. Two of them presented an acute myocardial infarction, whereas the third one showed thrombosis in the coronary microcirculation together with aortic valve disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
